# AI Development System Bootstrap for VS Code + GitHub Copilot

BOOTSTRAP NOTICE

This file is a one-time bootstrap specification used to generate an AI development support system for VS Code with GitHub Copilot.

After generation, the repository will contain documentation and navigation structures that allow Copilot to reason about the project architecture and development workflows.

The system enables AI to:

• Understand architecture automatically
• Navigate large repositories safely
• Avoid hallucinations
• Identify correct files before editing
• Respect architecture patterns
• Select relevant documentation context automatically

---------------------------------------------------------------------

GLOBAL DOCUMENT FORMAT

All generated documentation files must use `.md`.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

ROOT AGENT ENTRY FILE

Create a file at repository root:

AGENTS.md

Content:

For any development task, consult the project AI documentation inside `.ai/`.

Follow the workflows defined there before planning or implementing changes.

This ensures all AI interactions follow the structured system.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

COPILOT CONTEXT FILE

Create:

.github/copilot-instructions.md

Content must instruct Copilot to:

• Read architecture documentation
• Use file indexes to locate files
• Follow development workflows
• Respect architecture patterns
• Avoid editing files outside feature boundaries

